@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Hadith Al-Kisa";
    ViewData["Description"] = "The Hadith of the Cloak - Narration about the Five Pure Ones";
}

<div class="container my-5">
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-12">
            <h1 class="mb-4" style="color: #b90000; font-weight: 600;">Hadith Al-Kisa</h1>
            <p class="mb-4">The Hadith of the Cloak</p>

            <div class="alert alert-info mb-4">
                <i class="fas fa-info-circle"></i>
                <strong>Recitation Recommendation:</strong> Hadith Al-Kisa is commonly recited on Thursday nights
                and during the months of Muharram and Ramadan.
            </div>

            <section class="hadith-section mb-4 p-4 bg-white border">
                <h3 class="mb-3" style="color: #b90000;"><i class="fas fa-star"></i> About Hadith Al-Kisa</h3>
                    <p>
                        Hadith Al-Kisa (حديث الكساء) is a famous Islamic tradition narrated by Fatima Al-Zahra (SA),
                        the daughter of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH). The name "Al-Kisa" means "the cloak" in Arabic,
                        referring to the cloak that covered the Five Pure Ones (Ahl al-Kisa).
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        This hadith holds special significance as it identifies the members of Ahl al-Bayt (the
                        Prophet's household) and demonstrates their exalted status. It is considered one of the
                        most authentic and widely accepted narrations in Islamic tradition.
                    </p>
            </section>

            <section class="hadith-section mb-4 p-4 bg-white border">
                <h3 class="mb-3" style="color: #b90000;"><i class="fas fa-users"></i> The Five Pure Ones</h3>
                    <p>The narration describes five blessed personalities who were covered under the cloak:</p>
                    <ol class="lead">
                        <li><strong>Prophet Muhammad (PBUH)</strong> - The Messenger of Allah</li>
                        <li><strong>Imam Ali (AS)</strong> - The Commander of the Faithful</li>
                        <li><strong>Lady Fatima (SA)</strong> - The Chief of Women</li>
                        <li><strong>Imam Hassan (AS)</strong> - The Master of Youth of Paradise</li>
                        <li><strong>Imam Hussain (AS)</strong> - The Master of Martyrs</li>
                    </ol>
            </section>

            <section class="hadith-section mb-4 p-4 bg-white border">
                <h3 class="mb-3" style="color: #b90000;"><i class="fas fa-book-reader"></i> Summary of the Narration</h3>
                    <p>
                        Fatima Al-Zahra (SA) narrates that one day, when she was with her father Prophet Muhammad (PBUH),
                        he covered himself with a cloak from Khaybar. Then, one by one, Imam Hassan (AS), Imam Hussain (AS),
                        Imam Ali (AS), and finally Fatima herself joined him under the cloak.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        The Prophet (PBUH) then raised his hands and said: "O Allah! These are the People of my House
                        (Ahl al-Bayt). Remove all impurity from them and purify them with a thorough purification."
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        The angel Jibreel (Gabriel) descended and confirmed that Allah had indeed purified them and
                        elevated their status, as mentioned in the Verse of Purification (Ayat al-Tathir) from the Quran:
                    </p>
                    <div class="p-3 mt-3 text-center" style="background-color: #f8f9fa; border-left: 3px solid #b90000;">
                        <p class="mb-0">
                            <em>"Indeed, Allah intends to keep away impurity from you, O people of the household,
                            and purify you with a thorough purification."</em><br />
                            <strong>(Quran 33:33)</strong>
                        </p>
                    </div>
            </section>

            <section class="hadith-section mb-4 p-4 bg-white border">
                <h3 class="mb-3" style="color: #b90000;"><i class="fas fa-heart"></i> Benefits of Recitation</h3>
                    <p>According to narrations, reciting Hadith Al-Kisa brings numerous spiritual benefits:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Protection from calamities and difficulties</li>
                        <li>Forgiveness of sins</li>
                        <li>Fulfillment of legitimate needs</li>
                        <li>Increased blessings in sustenance</li>
                        <li>Strengthening connection with Ahl al-Bayt</li>
                        <li>Intercession on the Day of Judgment</li>
                    </ul>
            </section>

            <section class="hadith-section mb-4 p-4 bg-white border">
                <h3 class="mb-3" style="color: #b90000;"><i class="fas fa-download"></i> Resources</h3>
                <p>Access the complete text, audio, and translations:</p>
                <div class="d-flex gap-2 flex-wrap">
                    <a href="https://www.duas.org/kisa.htm" target="_blank" class="btn btn-sm" style="background-color: #b90000; color: white;">
                        <i class="fas fa-book"></i> Read Full Text
                    </a>
                    <a href="https://www.duas.org/kisa.htm" target="_blank" class="btn btn-sm" style="background-color: #b90000; color: white;">
                        <i class="fas fa-headphones"></i> Audio Recitation
                    </a>
                    <a href="https://www.duas.org/kisa.htm" target="_blank" class="btn btn-sm" style="background-color: #b90000; color: white;">
                        <i class="fas fa-language"></i> Translations
                    </a>
                </div>
            </section>

            <div class="alert alert-success">
                <i class="fas fa-lightbulb"></i>
                <strong>Recitation Tip:</strong> It is recommended to recite Hadith Al-Kisa with sincerity,
                reflection, and presence of heart. Taking time to understand its meanings enhances the spiritual
                benefits of this blessed narration.
            </div>

            <div class="text-center mt-4">
                <a asp-action="Duas" class="btn me-2" style="background-color: #b90000; color: white;">
                    <i class="fas fa-book"></i> View Other Duas
                </a>
                <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Index" class="btn" style="background-color: #666; color: white;">
                    <i class="fas fa-home"></i> Back to Home
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

